WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.100
Weights and Biases.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.100
The hosted tracker that deep learning teams love, and its standout feature is sweeps.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.733
Weights and Biases is a hosted tracker.

4
00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:15.700
Dashboards stream live, so you watch loss curves update mid-epoch from any browser.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.600
It has team reports and artifact versioning.

6
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.367
And its standout feature is sweeps, a managed hyperparameter search service.

7
00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:25.867
Here is the sweep loop.

8
00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:30.700
You declare a search space and a strategy: grid, random, or Bayesian.

9
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.433
The server suggests the next configuration.

10
00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:37.667
Any machine running an agent pulls it, trains, and reports back.

11
00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:43.333
Results flow into a parallel coordinates plot, showing which hyperparameters actually matter.

12
00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:46.000
Here is a sweep config.

13
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.722
The method is Bayesian.

14
00:00:47.722 --> 00:00:49.700
It could also be grid or random.

15
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.600
We want to maximize validation AUC.

16
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.700
And the search space covers learning rate and batch size.

17
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.367
The agent then runs thirty trainings, with a live dashboard.

18
00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:02.367
How does it compare with MLflow?

19
00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:08.133
W and B is hosted polish: zero setup, but your metrics live on their servers.

20
00:01:08.433 --> 00:01:12.333
MLflow is self-host control: your infrastructure, your data.

21
00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:19.767
Heavy deep learning teams often use W and B for research velocity, and MLflow for the production registry.

22
00:01:20.967 --> 00:01:25.033
Your CNN on light curves plateaus at point eight nine AUC.

23
00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:29.767
After days of hand-tuning, you run a thirty run Bayesian sweep overnight.

24
00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:37.300
The plot shows every run above point nine one has a learning rate between two e minus four and eight e minus four.

25
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.900
Two insights, one plot, no more debate.

26
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:41.959
Let's recap.

27
00:01:41.959 --> 00:01:45.467
W and B is a hosted tracker with live dashboards.

28
00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:48.100
Sweeps are managed hyperparameter search.

29
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.667
The parallel plot shows which settings matter.

30
00:01:50.967 --> 00:01:55.378
And the trade-off is hosted polish versus self-host control.

31
00:01:55.378 --> 00:01:56.333
Next up: DVC.
